<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">David of Trebizond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1408–<a href="/years/1463">1463</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as David Megas Komnenos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> was the last emperor of Trebizond, reigning from 1459. He sought a Christian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, but in 1461 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> besieged Trebizond and David surrendered it, ending the last Byzantine successor state. He was taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and executed with his sons in 1463.</p></div>
